WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.222
A set records membership without counting repeated copies or imposing an order

00:00:05.222 --> 00:00:08.034
These two sets share the element three

00:00:08.034 --> 00:00:15.267
The overlap shows shared membership, while the separate regions contain elements belonging to only one of the sets.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:20.630
Intersection keeps only elements that satisfy both membership conditions

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:25.144
Three belongs to A and to B, so it remains

00:00:25.144 --> 00:00:32.367
The word and corresponds to the overlap, helping us translate between set notation and logical conditions.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:37.310
Union includes elements belonging to at least one set

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:42.571
Adding the two set sizes counts three twice, so subtract the overlap once

00:00:42.571 --> 00:00:47.833
There are five distinct elements in the union; this correction prevents double counting.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:56.965
When sets are disjoint, their intersection is empty and no overlap correction is needed for their union's size

00:00:56.965 --> 00:01:05.667
Complements require another ingredient: a specified universe, because not in A only has meaning relative to the objects under consideration.
